# Slice 346 (the author 2026-11-10, LMX_blog/2026-11-10.md#receiver-args-only and #composed-form-breaks-structure): a
# receiver in the tail of a form declares inside it and never turns the outer name into a variable. The author's line
# `timeout: ms: int: time 500` declares the Structure timeout with the Structure ms inside and the place time in it --
# read and written through the path timeout\ms\time (here main\data\timeout\ms\time). `holder: int: time` is a
# Structure holder with the field time. `i: int: 5` and `x: 4` declare Structures with a value inside (one field each),
# no variable of an int.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and reads
# and writes the Structures by paths through main\data. main has no code, so there is no call: its part code is the
# empty `()`. The dump prints the description of main as written (time 500); the live value 7 is read by again.
sub: main () (
    timeout: ms: int: time 500
    holder: int: time
    i: int: 5
    x: 4
) ()
int: seen main\data\timeout\ms\time
main\data\timeout\ms\time := 7
int: again main\data\timeout\ms\time
int: n_i length(main\data\i)
int: n_x length(main\data\x)
